  "resident_configuration_change": "Agents adds AISOC_TENANT_SKILLS_KEYS_FILE and a separate read-only directory; existing organisation-memory credentials, env and mounts retained; no shared API token configured.",
  "authentication_contract": "Only the resolved/active skill GET changes to standard Bearer settings:read, tenant intersection and explicit transaction RLS. Each tenant has a dedicated skill reader with that scope only; no shared credential fallback. Other skill read/write/backtest/activation/retirement routes unchanged.",
  "read_contract": "Typed read status/failure/cache/expiry provenance with strict tenant/row validation. Cache identity includes URL and credential; expiry is checked on each live cache use and stale material is not adopted after a failed refresh. Empty active candidate set, no matching candidate and failed lookup remain distinct.",
  "selection_contract": "Preserves original additive rule20/technique10/source5/keyword2 selection, parent technique matching, first50 candidate bound and ID tie break. Records input, score, reasons, current selected version and actual sanitized/budgeted prompt guidance. Frozen replay uses split snapshot without live reads or current-date expiry, retaining skills_under_test exception.",
  "persistence_contract": "Skill read/selection and first-write skill artifact share the existing verdict transaction; artifact failure rolls it back and retry does not duplicate the artifact. Existing historical Run/artifacts and org-memory facts are not rewritten; full Run immutability is not claimed.",
  "fixture_contract": "Reuses A/B test tenants. Synthetic preactivated skill/current-version/history rows test only reading and selection. Four FK scaffolding replay rows explicitly have failed/probe_only/not_actual_backtest state and NULL scores/reports; no authoring, backtest or activation acceptance is claimed. Constraints remain enabled.",
  "scope_limitations": [
    "Resident automatic worker, graph, approvals and real responses stay disabled.",
    "KB, recent-disposition and identity reads remain separate work.",
    "Default 120-second cache does not guarantee immediate server-side retirement, edit or key revocation.",
    "Selected guidance and model consumption do not establish complete skill or investigation quality."
  ]
